# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites 3976 tracked files LF -> CRLF, which breaks the build and the test
# corpus in three separate ways:
#
#   * tests/**/*.out -- 1616 byte-exact goldens. The compat matrix compares guest
#     output against these verbatim (DOCS.md 8.2), so a trailing \r fails every
#     case that passes on Linux. This is silent: the diff looks identical.
#   * tests/**/*.tsv -- the case manifests. tools/matrix_runner.c splits on \t and
#     reads a fixed column count; \r lands inside the last field, which is the
#     disposition column that decides whether a case is active or excluded.
#   * tools/*.sh -- 20 scripts CMake invokes through HL_BASH_EXECUTABLE. A CRLF
#     shebang fails as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`.
#
# The engine's own build and test flow is LF throughout on every host, so LF is
# checked out on every host. Windows tooling in this repo (clang, CMake, Ninja,
# MSYS2 bash, PowerShell) all read LF correctly; nothing here needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Guest fixtures and prebuilt artifacts: never touched, never diffed as text.
# Git already infers -text for these, but inference reads the first 8000 bytes,
# and a cross-built guest ELF whose header happens to be NUL-free would be
# misclassified and silently corrupted. Naming them is cheap insurance.
*.a           binary
*.o           binary
*.tar.gz      binary
*.exe         binary
*.dll         binary
*.lib         binary
*.pdb         binary

pkgs/rust/assets/lib/**   binary
pkgs/rust/testdata/**     binary

# Cross-built static-glibc guest binaries, committed without an extension.
tests/compat/isa/**            binary
tests/compat/core/regress/go_cgo_stackgrow_arm  binary

# Checkpoint images are captured guest memory: byte-exact by definition.
*.ckpt        binary
